1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,264
Now the class keyword. This problem is worth 34 to

2
00:00:03,364 --> 00:00:06,830
40 points, and it checks a specific list of features:

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:12,212
private fields, a static counter, getters and setters, toPrimitive, inheritance,

4
00:00:12,312 --> 00:00:15,308
and custom errors. Let's go through every one.

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,688
Here's a Bike class. A static field belongs to the class

6
00:00:20,788 --> 00:00:23,775
itself, not to each bike. We'll use it to count how

7
00:00:23,875 --> 00:00:27,164
many bikes were created. The hash sign makes it private.

8
00:00:27,233 --> 00:00:31,023
These two are private instance fields. The hash is part of the name,

9
00:00:31,123 --> 00:00:34,513
and you have to declare them in the class body before you use

10
00:00:34,613 --> 00:00:37,717
them. Only code inside the class can read or write them.

11
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,810
The constructor takes default parameters, just like a

12
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:43,628
function, and stores them in the private fields.

13
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:46,658
Then it bumps the counter. Notice it's Bike dot hash

14
00:00:46,758 --> 00:00:49,657
total, not this dot hash total. Statics live on the

15
00:00:49,757 --> 00:00:52,480
class, so you reach them through the class name.

16
00:00:52,866 --> 00:00:57,331
Exam trap. Trying to read b dot hash color from outside the class is

17
00:00:57,431 --> 00:01:02,030
a syntax error. If outside code needs the value, you provide a getter.

18
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:07,786
A getter looks like a method with get in front,

19
00:01:07,886 --> 00:01:10,869
but you use it like a property, with no parentheses.

20
00:01:10,969 --> 00:01:13,952
b dot color runs this and returns the private color.

21
00:01:14,033 --> 00:01:18,016
A setter runs when you assign. b dot price equals 300 calls

22
00:01:18,116 --> 00:01:22,515
this with p equal to 300. The exam almost always wants validation

23
00:01:22,615 --> 00:01:27,637
here: only store the value if it's positive. Otherwise, quietly ignore it.

24
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:30,254
A static method is called on the class,

25
00:01:30,354 --> 00:01:32,673
Bike dot getTotal, not on an object.

26
00:01:32,766 --> 00:01:35,985
And returning this from a method lets you chain calls,

27
00:01:36,085 --> 00:01:39,242
like paint blue, then paint green, in one expression.

28
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:45,238
This is the course's version of Java's toString. The method's

29
00:01:45,338 --> 00:01:48,579
name is the symbol Symbol dot toPrimitive, which is why

30
00:01:48,679 --> 00:01:51,920
it's in square brackets. Whenever the object is used in

31
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:55,261
a template literal or with plus, JavaScript calls this.

32
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:57,919
The double dollar sign is just a literal dollar

33
00:01:58,019 --> 00:02:01,233
sign, followed by the dollar-brace that inserts the price.

34
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:04,045
Now let's use it. We make a red bike for

35
00:02:04,145 --> 00:02:07,209
250, then try to set the price to negative 5.

36
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,140
Then a valid price, two chained paints, and print

37
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:12,720
again with the getter and the static count.

38
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:16,890
The negative price was rejected by the setter, so it still

39
00:02:16,990 --> 00:02:20,513
says 250. After the update and the chain, it's a green

40
00:02:20,613 --> 00:02:23,800
bike for 300, and exactly one bike has been made.

41
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:30,580
Two classic output questions. Bike has a setter for price, but

42
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:33,568
no getter. So what does reading b dot price give?

43
00:02:33,666 --> 00:02:35,887
And color has a getter but no setter. So

44
00:02:35,987 --> 00:02:38,150
what happens when we assign pink to it?

45
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:42,922
Reading price gives undefined, because there's no getter to run. And the

46
00:02:43,022 --> 00:02:47,162
assignment to color is ignored, so it's still green. In strict mode,

47
00:02:47,262 --> 00:02:51,153
or in a module, that assignment would throw a TypeError instead.

48
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:55,121
Exam trap. A setter with no getter reads as

49
00:02:55,221 --> 00:02:58,805
undefined. A getter with no setter can't be assigned.

50
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:06,576
Inheritance: EBike extends Bike and adds its own private range.

51
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:10,300
In the child's constructor, call super first. super runs the

52
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:14,033
parent constructor, which sets color and price and bumps the

53
00:03:14,133 --> 00:03:16,646
counter. Only after that can you use this.

54
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:19,816
To override a method and still reuse the parent's

55
00:03:19,916 --> 00:03:23,455
version, call super dot info. Bike's info returns color,

56
00:03:23,555 --> 00:03:25,729
then bike, and we append the range.

57
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:28,004
Then we make a white e-bike and print it.

58
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:32,138
The override works. toPrimitive is inherited, so the template

59
00:03:32,238 --> 00:03:35,159
literal still prints nicely. And the total is 2,

60
00:03:35,259 --> 00:03:38,620
because the e-bike went through Bike's constructor too.

61
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,902
Exam trap. Touching this before calling super throws a

62
00:03:43,002 --> 00:03:46,388
ReferenceError. And a child class can't read the parent's

63
00:03:46,488 --> 00:03:49,445
private hash fields, which is why EBike uses super

64
00:03:49,545 --> 00:03:52,320
dot info instead of reading the color directly.

65
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:58,815
Older exams also ask for a custom error. Extend Error,

66
00:03:58,915 --> 00:04:02,200
pass the message to super, which sets e dot message,

67
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:04,804
and set this dot name to the class name.

68
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:07,536
Then throw it when a value is out of range.

69
00:04:07,633 --> 00:04:11,650
In the try block, the first call works. The second call throws,

70
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:15,309
so the line after it never runs. Control jumps to catch.

71
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:17,879
Catch prints the name and the message, and

72
00:04:17,979 --> 00:04:21,012
checks instanceof. And finally runs no matter what.

73
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:25,080
So we get 20, then DataRangeError colon Speed 45 out of

74
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:29,547
range, then true true, because the error is both a DataRangeError

75
00:04:29,647 --> 00:04:33,396
and an Error, and finally, done. Never is never printed.

76
00:04:36,466 --> 00:04:40,915
Practice question 1. Write a Ticket class with a private seat, a private

77
00:04:41,015 --> 00:04:45,148
static count, a constructor with default seat G A and price 20 that

78
00:04:45,248 --> 00:04:49,760
bumps the count, a seat getter, a price setter that only accepts positive

79
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:54,752
values, a static getCount, and toPrimitive so the template literal gives Seat G

80
00:04:54,852 --> 00:04:57,342
A, dollar 20. Pause the video and try it.

81
00:05:05,633 --> 00:05:09,813
Declare the static count and the private fields first. The constructor

82
00:05:09,913 --> 00:05:13,482
stores both values and does Ticket dot hash count plus plus.

83
00:05:13,582 --> 00:05:17,211
The getter returns the seat. The setter checks p greater than

84
00:05:17,311 --> 00:05:21,920
zero before storing. getCount is static. And toPrimitive returns the template

85
00:05:22,020 --> 00:05:25,405
string, with a double dollar sign for the literal dollar.

86
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:33,643
Practice question 2. Using that Ticket class, which has only a getter

87
00:05:33,743 --> 00:05:37,272
for seat, what does this print? Pause the video and try it.

88
00:05:45,566 --> 00:05:48,883
G A, B 12, and 2. Assigning A 1 to t1 dot seat

89
00:05:48,983 --> 00:05:54,007
does nothing, because there's no setter, so t1 keeps the default G A.

90
00:05:54,107 --> 00:05:58,018
And the static count went up once for each new Ticket.

91
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:05,840
Recap. Private fields with a hash, a static counter bumped with

92
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:10,168
the class name in the constructor, getters and setters with validation,

93
00:06:10,268 --> 00:06:14,680
static methods, and return this for chaining. Symbol dot toPrimitive makes

94
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:19,252
template literals print your object. For inheritance, call super first, and

95
00:06:19,352 --> 00:06:22,849
use super dot method to reuse the parent. And custom errors

96
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:24,800
extend Error and set their name.

